      "writtenOn": "2023-09-20T22:58:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think Michael\u0027s intention was to keep all rendering algorithm decisions in `Device::chooseRenderer`. I added `DrawContext::getOrCreatePathAtlas` because I needed to scope the ownership of PathAtlas\u0027es to be per Device/DrawContext due to their interactions with flushes when there are multiple Devices: https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/719316. `DrawContext` just happened to be a good place to store a `PathAtlas` as it seems to generally own \"pending recording data\" until tasks get snapped.\n\nI think we could evolve this to be less opinionated about which atlas gets selected. Maybe there should be methods such as `getComputePathAtlas`, `getSoftwarePathAtlas` (which can return nullptr if the particular atlas type is not supported) and the logic about which one to use remains in `Device::chooseRenderer`?",
      "revId": "bd224ed4abf2d8eca4238994271c4425a88cb05e",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    }
